Johnny Skyfall is a half-elf man in [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]], friendly and profane, who wears dark glasses and a jean jacket and plays music wherever he goes. He is the Party's talker. He lies easily, hands out false names (Jonathan Skyfall, Dave Fuller, Salvado Van Warhol, Jonathan Scaff), and is the one sent in when a door has to be talked open. Words are his whole trade, and the red choker taken off [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]] lets him speak and write the tongue of demons.

Before the Midnight Sun he kept a tavern called The Last Stop in a border town, and his whole family died on the Night of the Midnight Sun. He was telling a story in the tavern when the world froze and the sky went black. The [[Divinity/Outer Gods/Watcher With 1,000 Eyes|Watcher]] had come to hear the end of the story, and the two struck a bargain: each time Johnny dies, he returns and tells the Watcher what he has learned of people. He has died and been brought back many times since. One was the attack on the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]], when he came back by way of [[Aut]] and left a piece of himself in the [[Pharos]]. Aut later called that piece back into him, and he carries Aut's mark. Aut has since broken with the Party for going to the [[Divinity/The Narrative/Menhir|Menhir]] instead of him, and the mark burned on Johnny when he did. The [[People/Sharp the Cunning Man|Cunning Man]] found him only tenuously settled in his own body. The death before that, he heard the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] instead of the Watcher, and he has not been able to reach his god since. The [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Machine God|Machine God]] of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]'s lower hull has since brought him back from the dead.

He keeps a black chess piece on a necklace through which he speaks to a [[Org/Ghosts of Raelion|Ghost]] named Red, and he counts the Ghost [[People/Donnie|Donnie]] an old friend. Through the Ghosts he reaches the [[Org/Sable and Suns/index|Sable and Suns]] and other dealers in the city.

He travels with [[People/Benny|Benny]], [[People/Anzu|Anzu]], [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] and [[People/Sir Arctos|Sir Arctos]], and makes himself useful at the [[Sin and Tonic]] between jobs. Over the Party's six months of downtime he taught improv classes and hunted for a way past the wall of fire into [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]].
